- `precedence(n6, n8)`, `precedence(n7, n9)` and downstream paths to `e1`/`e2`: Control-flow logic contradicts the stated end condition. The source states "The process ends when the Goods are sent or when the Invoice is sent," but the model mandates execution through "Mark as Sent" and "End" actions before reaching any terminal node. (SMC4, SMC5)